# Cloudflare Pages headers — Shikkha24
#
# Source: docs/security.md §5 (security headers + CSP).
#
# TWO CSP PROFILES (docs/security.md §5): a strict one for static / editorial
# pages, and a relaxed one for ad-bearing pages, because AdSense needs inline
# scripts and dynamic script injection.
#
# ⚠️ Cloudflare Pages does NOT override a duplicated header — **it joins the
# values with a comma**, and a comma-joined CSP is enforced as two policies, so
# the strict `script-src 'self'` would still block AdSense. A more specific rule
# therefore has to DETACH the inherited value first (`! Content-Security-Policy`)
# and then set its own. Verified against the Pages headers documentation
# 2026-09-12.
#
# ⚠️ **S12 check:** confirm in production that an ad-bearing page returns exactly
# ONE Content-Security-Policy header. If the detach does not take effect the
# header will contain a comma, AdSense will be blocked, and this must be resolved
# by moving the CSP into a Pages Function instead.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  # `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` is required by Astro's inline stylesheets
  # (`build.inlineStylesheets: 'auto'` in astro.config.mjs). It is the only
  # relaxation in this profile — scripts stay strict.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://media.shikkha24.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; media-src 'self' https://media.shikkha24.com; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Relaxed profile — the three routes that carry ad slots (S7).
#
# Exactly the pages where `AdSlot` renders: the homepage, article pages and
# category listings. Every other route keeps the strict policy, which is the
# point of having two profiles at all.
#
# The AdSense loader in `AdCreative.astro` only injects the library when a real
# AdSense unit exists, so today — with no unit configured — these routes still
# make zero third-party requests. The relaxation costs nothing until ads ship.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://media.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.gstatic.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; media-src 'self' https://media.shikkha24.com; frame-src https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/article/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://media.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.gstatic.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; media-src 'self' https://media.shikkha24.com; frame-src https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/category/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://media.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.gstatic.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; media-src 'self' https://media.shikkha24.com; frame-src https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Hashed build assets are content-addressed — cache them forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted fonts are content-stable; re-fetching them is pure waste.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML must revalidate so a publish is visible as soon as the batch window closes.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
